# Site-wide security response headers for Netlify.
#
# public/ is Astro's static asset dir — everything in it is copied
# byte-for-byte into the build output (dist/, per astro.config.mjs's
# default publicDir/outDir and netlify.toml's `publish = "dist"`),
# confirmed locally via `npm run build` (dist/_headers matches this file
# exactly). Netlify reads _headers from the publish directory root and
# applies the `/*` block to every response by default.
#
# CSP notes (see the security review that accompanies this file for the
# full per-directive reasoning):
#   - This is a fully static site (Astro `output: "static"`, no adapter,
#     no per-request server) built once and served as prebuilt files, so
#     there is no request-time hook to mint a fresh nonce. A nonce baked
#     in at build time would be identical on every page load and would
#     provide no real protection, so it is not used here.
#   - script-src and style-src both need 'unsafe-inline': the theme
#     bootstrap script, the GTM/GA bootstrap snippets (src/layouts/Layout.astro),
#     and marp-core's rendered slide decks (inline <style> per deck, inline
#     style="" attributes, and an inline <script> from
#     @marp-team/marpit-svg-polyfill) all rely on it. The GTM/GA snippet
#     content is interpolated with PUBLIC_GTM_ID/PUBLIC_GA_MEASUREMENT_ID at
#     build time via Astro's define:vars, so it differs per environment and
#     can't be pinned to a static sha256 hash in this non-templated file.
#     Do NOT add a hash-source here without also adding 'unsafe-inline'
#     removal awareness: CSP3 browsers drop 'unsafe-inline' entirely the
#     moment *any* hash/nonce source is present on the same directive,
#     which would silently break every unhashed inline script (GTM/GA) the
#     next time this file is touched.
#   - 'unsafe-eval' is deliberately NOT included — nothing in this build
#     (Astro static output, Svelte islands compiled ahead of time) needs it.
#   - img-src allows https://raw.githubusercontent.com: the vendored Marp
#     Wave theme (src/styles/marp-themes/wave.css) loads its background
#     wave graphic from there via a CSS background-image url(), which CSP
#     governs under img-src, not style-src.
/*
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=63072000
  Permissions-Policy: accelerometer=(), camera=(), geolocation=(), gyroscope=(), magnetometer=(), microphone=(), payment=(), usb=(), interest-cohort=(), browsing-topics=(), fullscreen=(self)
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline' https://*.googletagmanager.com; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline' https://fonts.googleapis.com; font-src 'self' https://fonts.gstatic.com; img-src 'self' data: https://www.gravatar.com https://raw.githubusercontent.com https://*.google-analytics.com https://*.googletagmanager.com; connect-src 'self' https://*.google-analytics.com https://*.analytics.google.com https://*.googletagmanager.com https://*.ingest.sentry.io https://*.ingest.us.sentry.io https://*.ingest.de.sentry.io; frame-src 'self' https://*.googletagmanager.com; object-src 'none'; base-uri 'self'; form-action 'self'; frame-ancestors 'none'
